<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalfun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalfun was the leader of the Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> soldiers, probably from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, who seized the southern Italian port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> around 847. Some of them had served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> for the rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> and Salerno. He is regarded as the first ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bari, though he does not seem to have held the title of emir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalfun.jpg" alt="Kalfun" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: from the Middle Ages, unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MadridSkylitzesFol97ra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
